import H0mework.Physics.Matter.ConjugateMatterVariation

/-!
# S9-C3c1a: primitive matter variation and weak adjoint equation

The independent matter field is varied through the actual
`matterCoordinateEquiv` coordinates.  Its first jet is regenerated by
Fréchet differentiation together with the primitive Lorentz and P286
connections, so the action mouth accepts neither a derivative variation nor
an adjoint Dirac equation receipt.

The common local and integrated action are proved exactly affine for every
compactly supported smooth matter variation.  Continuity, compact support,
and integrability of the first density are generated internally.  Action
stationarity therefore yields the genuine derivative-on-variation weak
equation; integration by parts and its pointwise adjoint equation are kept for
the next checkpoint.
-/

